accTitle: Planning-side structured rollout and committed simulated-world transition
accDescr: The same pure SupplyChainSimulator is used in two different paths. During planning, SimulatorBackedPlanningWorldModel applies a typed action to an isolated PlanningState branch and returns a candidate next state without committing the current environment. During grounding, an action handler passes the command through SupplyChainSimulationWorld, whose adapter checks the expected snapshot version, invokes the simulator, and compare-and-set commits the returned snapshot as the new current simulated world.
    subgraph CandidatePath[Planning-side structured simulator rollout]
      Candidate[Candidate action and PlanningState]
      PlanningModel[SimulatorBackedPlanningWorldModel]
      CandidateBranch[Next PlanningState branch]
      Candidate --> PlanningModel
      PlanningModel -->|simulate candidate command| Simulator
      Simulator --> CandidateBranch
    end
    subgraph GroundingPath[Grounding action against the current modeled environment]
      Request[Authorized typed grounding request]
      Dispatcher[ActionDispatcher and handler precondition]
      WorldPort[SupplyChainSimulationWorld port]
      Adapter[In-memory world adapter]
      Current[Current SupplyChainSnapshot]
      Version{Expected version current?}
      Result[SimulationResult]
      Commit[Atomic compare-and-set]
      NewCurrent[New current snapshot and typed effects]
      Conflict[Typed conflict; reload and reconsider]
      Request --> Dispatcher --> WorldPort --> Adapter
      Adapter --> Current
      Adapter --> Version
      Version -->|No| Conflict
      Version -->|Yes| Simulator
      Simulator --> Result
      Result --> Commit
      Commit -->|Committed| NewCurrent
      Commit -->|Lost race| Conflict
    end
    classDef pure fill:#e9f2ff,stroke:#24558a,color:#152b45
    classDef state fill:#f0f5ec,stroke:#547a3a,color:#20351a
    classDef control fill:#fff4df,stroke:#9c6a18,color:#4d3510
    class Simulator pure
    class CandidateBranch,NewCurrent state
    class Version,Dispatcher,Commit control
